{
  "requirement": "The `trust-but-verify` crate's `outline` module provides language selection,\nsource outlining, selector resolution, and source structural hashes.\nApplications can use these operations directly on files and supplied source\nsnapshots.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "structural: The only structural obligation in `requirements.sdk.outlines.independent` is placement and ownership. The `trust-but-verify` crate's `outline` module must provide language selection, source outlining, selector resolution, and structural hashes. It must offer them directly on files and on supplied source snapshots. The rest of the text is behavioral.\n\nA root that omitted this module, or that put these operations only behind another module such as the agent or request layers, would break this clause. A different internal factoring of the helpers would not.\n\nThe supplied root `crates/trust-but-verify/src/lib.rs#mod[outline]` carries the `{impl}` marker. It is the `pub mod outline`, mapped by `#[path]` to `outline/contents.rs`. That file supplies each required operation:\n- **Language selection:** `OutlineContent::parse_source` in `outline/contents.rs` calls `languages::registry().for_path` and falls back to `languages::PlainText`. The bundled languages sit in the `pub mod languages` child module. `OutlineLang` is the language-rule trait, and `OutlineContent::from_path_with` and `from_source_with` take a caller-supplied language.\n- **Source outlining:** `OutlineContent::from_path`, `from_source` and `from_id` build the content. `OutlineContent::outline` returns the `Outline`.\n- **Selector resolution:** `OutlineContent::select` resolves a selector, and the child module `pub mod selector` supports it.\n- **Structural hashes:** `OutlineContent::structural_hash` and `fingerprint_scheme` expose them.\n- **Files and supplied snapshots:** `from_path` reads a file. `from_source` takes an `Arc<str>` snapshot and does not read the named file.\n\nThe root fully covers the structural obligation, and the other items in this module are reached from it.\n\nbehavioral: The requirement says the `outline` module offers language selection, source outlining, selector resolution and source structural hashes. It also says applications can use these directly on files and on supplied source snapshots. The tests import everything from `trust_but_verify::outline` (`OutlineContent`, `OutlineData`, `languages`, `OutlineLang`) and cover each operation.\n\n- **Language selection**\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs#fn[file_constructors_infer_the_language_and_return_addressed_contents]` writes `AUTH.RS` and checks that the language is inferred as `rust-structural-v1`. The extension is uppercase, so the match is case-insensitive.\n  - `fn[selected_contents_outlive_handles_and_later_file_edits]` uses `notes.unknown`. The fallback gives plain-text line items, and its fingerprint scheme ends in `:own-v1`.\n  - `fn[bundled_languages_claim_extensions_and_supply_the_same_public_outline]` checks each bundled language's extensions, name and fingerprint scheme. It also checks that `PlainText` claims no extensions.\n- **Source outlining**\n  - The `fn[file_constructors_infer_the_language_and_return_addressed_contents]` test asserts the exact outline selectors `[\"\", \"fn[check_token]\"]`.\n  - The `fn[selected_contents_outlive_handles_and_later_file_edits]` test asserts that the outline has 3 items.\n  - The bundled-languages test checks the selector for one item in each language.\n- **Selector resolution**\n  - `OutlineContent::from_id` and `select` resolve `fn[check_token]`, and the resolved text is asserted.\n  - The root selector `\"\"` is resolved and its text asserted.\n  - A selection made after the file has changed fails, as the test expects.\n- **Structural hashes**\n  - The tests assert that `fingerprint()` and `structural_hash()` agree, and that the fingerprint scheme is the expected one.\n  - They also assert that fingerprints stay stable after the handle is dropped and the file is edited.\n- **Files and supplied snapshots**\n  - `from_path` and `from_source` are both used. The test asserts their root fingerprints are equal, and that selecting `fn[check_token]` through the file and through the snapshot gives equal fingerprints.\n  - The snapshot-independence test asserts that retained content does not change when the file is edited.\n\nThe requirement is an umbrella statement of capability, not a list of detailed rules. Detailed cases such as errors, duplicates and Unicode have their own requirements and tests, and those are outside this assessment. I found no unchecked obligation.",
  "references": "da2fb84f0ff55fd351711078b02a047f2b0d97d63ce1443982f82f1be0922eaf",
