        "rationale": "The only structural obligation in `requirements.sdk.outlines.independent` is placement and ownership. The `trust-but-verify` crate's `outline` module must provide language selection, source outlining, selector resolution, and structural hashes. It must offer them directly on files and on supplied source snapshots. The rest of the text is behavioral.\n\nA root that omitted this module, or that put these operations only behind another module such as the agent or request layers, would break this clause. A different internal factoring of the helpers would not.\n\nThe supplied root `crates/trust-but-verify/src/lib.rs#mod[outline]` carries the `{impl}` marker. It is the `pub mod outline`, mapped by `#[path]` to `outline/contents.rs`. That file supplies each required operation:\n- **Language selection:** `OutlineContent::parse_source` in `outline/contents.rs` calls `languages::registry().for_path` and falls back to `languages::PlainText`. The bundled languages sit in the `pub mod languages` child module. `OutlineLang` is the language-rule trait, and `OutlineContent::from_path_with` and `from_source_with` take a caller-supplied language.\n- **Source outlining:** `OutlineContent::from_path`, `from_source` and `from_id` build the content. `OutlineContent::outline` returns the `Outline`.\n- **Selector resolution:** `OutlineContent::select` resolves a selector, and the child module `pub mod selector` supports it.\n- **Structural hashes:** `OutlineContent::structural_hash` and `fingerprint_scheme` expose them.\n- **Files and supplied snapshots:** `from_path` reads a file. `from_source` takes an `Arc<str>` snapshot and does not read the named file.\n\nThe root fully covers the structural obligation, and the other items in this module are reached from it."
